qe(q,'sync-classic-problems-q2','workedExample','If these rates persist, the backlog grows by 30000 lines/s: 108 million lines in an hour. At an illustrative 200 bytes per line, payload alone is 21.6 GB before object/queue overhead. Memory pressure may cause allocation failures, termination or reduced throughput; a kill is not inevitable. A bounded queue applies back-pressure, with bounded queued item count rather than a universal byte limit.','MathcorrectbutOOMkillinevitablefalse anditemsizebound.',py)
